TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"authorizedComments":[{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \"no commit needed\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z","id":2,"updatedAt":"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z","url":"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2"},{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER STEER (seq 8, commit-discipline — tally#622 family). Your verification was CORRECT: the instruments deliverables already landed on main via ancestor 4b1d714 and acceptance passes. But the spec-build driver REJECTS a zero-diff squash (\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\", exit 1) — three attempts have already looped this way. A no-new-commit conclusion can never complete this lane. Required: after re-verifying acceptance, land exactly one small NON-EMPTY commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your ownership paths (container/rootfs and tests). Preferred shape: add tests/RECONCILE-instruments-2026-08-30.md — a short note recording the reconcile (HEAD at verification, acceptance command result: py_compile x3, 11 tests, repo suite 50 OK, and that deliverables arrived via ancestor 4b1d714). Do NOT use --allow-empty (the squash still stages no change and fails identically); do NOT touch results/receipts/ or any path outside your ownership; do NOT rewrite the three overlay modules. Then finish normally.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-30T03:50:26.513Z","id":1,"updatedAt":"2026-08-30T03:50:26.513Z","url":"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/1"}],"receipt":{"lateRecheckCommentIds":[],"preparedCommentIds":[2,1],"recheckTruncated":false,"rechecked":true,"source":{"kind":"local-jsonl","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl","preparedCursor":2,"recheckedCursor":2,"registrationId":"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff"}},"taskId":"instruments"}
